      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(canvas): surface eval errors instead of silently swallowing them",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `canvas.eval` returns a non-string result or error from the node (e.g. `{ payload: { error: \"SyntaxError\" } }`), the old code returned `jsonResult({ ok: true })` — a generic success signal. The agent sees success even when the JavaScript evaluation failed.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe `raw` cast only recognized `{ payload?: { result?: string } }`. When `result` was absent or non-string, control fell through to generic success. Errors and non-string values were silently discarded.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Error checked first: if `payload.error` is a string, return `{ ok: false, error }`\n- String results unchanged (text content with details)\n- Non-string results (number, object, explicit null) use `\"result\" in payload` presence check — surfaced as `{ ok: true, result }`\n- Void eval (no result prop, no error) returns `{ ok: true }`\n\nFiles changed:\n- `extensions/canvas/src/tool.ts`: Refactored `case \"eval\"` handler with `\"result\" in` check\n- `extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts`: Added regression test for explicit null\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: Eval errors surfaced; explicit null preserved; successful non-string results visible to agent\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `git diff --check` — clean\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts` — 13 passed, 1 skipped\n  - New test: \"surfaces an explicit null eval result\"\n  - Head: `b8eb5163554`\n",
        "branch": "fix/canvas-eval-silent-failure",
        "head_sha": "b8eb516355499e65f01e9661c50a200f4ea30c72",
